# StationIdentity wave (Content.Server/_Solreign/StationIdentity/) — locale for the shared
# ambient-identity engine's mood popups, and the two weather-style events it references.

## SolreignSolarFlareRule
station-event-solreign-solar-flare-start-announcement = Sensors report a brief solar flare washing over the station. Expect a flicker.
station-event-solreign-solar-flare-end-announcement = The flare has passed. Power readings are back to normal.

## SolreignSporeDriftRule
station-event-solreign-spore-drift-start-announcement = Atmospherics reports a harmless drift of bioluminescent spore in the station's air currents.
station-event-solreign-spore-drift-end-announcement = The spore drift has settled.
solreign-spore-drift-glow-popup = A mote of spore glows softly as it drifts past.

## SolreignAcidStormRule (wow-wiring wave) — corporate-euphemism framing throughout: an external
## atmospheric contaminant event, not body horror. Never "melting" or "burning" imagery.
station-event-solreign-acid-storm-start-announcement = Atmospherics reports an external contaminant plume moving across the hull. Neutralizing agents deployed; minor visual haze expected. Solreign appreciates your patience.
station-event-solreign-acid-storm-end-announcement = Contaminant levels have returned to standard parameters. Thank you for your continued cooperation.
solreign-acid-storm-glow-popup = A bead of acid-green condensation drifts past on the air current.

## SolreignStationMoodComponent ambient popups (SolreignOasis)
solreign-station-mood-popup-1 = The station hums, faint and steady, like it's breathing with you.
solreign-station-mood-popup-2 = Somewhere overhead, the light shifts a shade — barely enough to notice.
solreign-station-mood-popup-3 = For a moment, the corridor feels less like metal and more like a held breath.
